From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: rkisp1: support the rk3566/rk3568 V21 ISP

The rk3566/rk3568 ISP ("V21") reports media-device hardware revision 15.
The kernel rkisp1 driver treats its statistics and parameters blocks as
V12-compatible (same grid and histogram sizes), differing from V12 only
in that the sensor data arrives through a CSI2RX host receiver, which is
handled entirely in the kernel. The IPA therefore only needs the V12
hardware settings for this revision.

Add the RKISP1_V21 enumerator to the bundled uAPI header and select the
V12 hardware settings for it, so the IPA initialises instead of failing
with "Hardware revision 15 is currently not supported" and the PineTab2
rear camera (ov5648) can stream through the hardware ISP.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff --git a/include/linux/rkisp1-config.h b/include/linux/rkisp1-config.h
index 3e8aa77fd..90ebaebb8 100644
--- a/include/linux/rkisp1-config.h
+++ b/include/linux/rkisp1-config.h
@@ -197,6 +197,8 @@
  *	histogram as v12.
  * @RKISP1_V_IMX8MP: Used in at least i.MX8MP. Same number of entries in grids
  *	and histogram as v10.
+ * @RKISP1_V21: Used in RK3566 and RK3568. Same number of entries in grids and
+ *	histogram as v12; the ISP receives through a CSI2RX host on these SoCs.
  */
 enum rkisp1_cif_isp_version {
 	RKISP1_V10 = 10,
@@ -204,6 +206,7 @@ enum rkisp1_cif_isp_version {
 	RKISP1_V12,
 	RKISP1_V13,
 	RKISP1_V_IMX8MP,
+	RKISP1_V21,
 };
 
 enum rkisp1_cif_isp_histogram_mode {
diff --git a/src/ipa/rkisp1/rkisp1.cpp b/src/ipa/rkisp1/rkisp1.cpp
index 58ef163d8..2f2b81d9a 100644
--- a/src/ipa/rkisp1/rkisp1.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/rkisp1/rkisp1.cpp
@@ -150,6 +150,7 @@ int IPARkISP1::init(const IPASettings &settings, unsigned int hwRevision,
 		context_.hw = ipaHwSettingsIMX8MP;
 		break;
 	case RKISP1_V12:
+	case RKISP1_V21:
 		context_.hw = ipaHwSettingsV12;
 		break;
 	default:
